  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ghana &#x2013; Expansion of services to plant breeding and plant production companies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a loan from DGGF, Iribov Holding B.V. will be able to expand their current activities in Ghana by building a new laboratory and greenhouses. The company provides services (tissue culture and nursery) to plant breeding and plant production companies from the Netherlands and other countries, including Ghana. The investment will contribute to the creation of around 200 new jobs in Ghana, of which approximately 75% will be filled by women. This number may increase if sales in West Africa increase. In the long term, local services can also contribute to food security. Furthermore, the company has an action plan to not only visualize its carbon footprint, but also to reduce it.And finally, this investment will have a positive impact on the Dutch economy, as Dutch technology will be supplied for the expansion in Ghana and some jobs will be created in the Netherlands.</narrative>
  </description>
